# Quality gate (before merge / push)

Ship clean diffs. Agents must self-check before calling work done.

## Required checks (touched areas)

```bash
npm run lint
npm run format:check
npm run typecheck          # when TS / packages / shared types change
npm run test:api           # when apps/api behavior changes
npm run test:api:e2e       # when HTTP routes / auth / contracts change
npm run test:packages      # when api-client / contract change
npm run test:e2e           # when user-facing web flows / i18n change
```

Do not push knowing lint/typecheck/tests are red. Fix or add focused tests in the same change set (see testing rule).

## Diff hygiene — reject leftover process junk

Remove before commit:

- `console.log` / `debugger` / temporary `TODO: remove` scaffolding
- Commented-out code blocks and dead exports
- Unused imports, unused deps added “just in case”
- Orphan files from experiments (`foo.old.ts`, `test2.tsx`, scratch notes in src)
- Secrets, `.env`, credentials, personal paths
- Drive-by reformatting of unrelated files

## Consistency

- Match existing folder patterns (do not invent a parallel component system)
- Same problem → same solution (auth, validation, storage, i18n, api-client)
- Naming: clear English identifiers; UI strings via messages, not hardcoded
- After contract changes: `npm run build:packages` and update callers

## Performance sanity (lightweight review)

- No unbounded `findMany` / unpaginated feeds
- No fetching the same resource repeatedly in a loop (client or server)
- No giant client bundles for simple pages (keep heavy UI behind client boundaries intentionally)
- Images/files go through established storage/upload paths

## PR / commit shape

- One concern per commit when practical (Conventional Commits)
- Behavior change ⇒ tests
- Prefer small PRs over “redesign everything” dumps
